+### 1.1 Server Context Digest
+
+`instructions` from `initialize` / `server/discover` is natural-language guidance that the
+client may place in the model context. It is not part of any `Tool` object, so the digest in
+section 1 does not cover it. `serverInfo.name` and `serverInfo.version` likewise identify
+the surface that was observed but are not part of a `Tool`.
+
+A host that pins SHOULD compute a Server Context Digest over:
+
+1. `serverInfo.name` (string; empty if absent),
+2. `serverInfo.version` (string; empty if absent),
+3. `instructions` (string; absent normalized to `""`),
+
+serialized with RFC 8785 and hashed with SHA-256, in the same `sha256:` form. The host MUST
+store this digest with the tool pins and MUST re-check it whenever it re-checks
+`tools/list`. A changed instructions string is a mismatch even when every Tool digest is
+unchanged. A host that presents `instructions` to the model MUST NOT present a changed
+value until it is approved under host policy.
+
+`serverInfo.title`, if present, is display metadata and is not part of this digest.
+
 ### 2. Tool Set Digest (optional)
 
 To compare whole servers, the Tool Set Digest is SHA-256 over the RFC 8785 serialization of
 the array of Tool Definition Digest strings for every tool in the result, sorted by tool
 `name`, in the same `sha256:` form. It is computed after all pages of a paginated result are
-collected.
+collected. The Tool Set Digest covers `Tool` objects only; it does not cover `serverInfo` or
+`instructions` (see section 1.1).
 
