+The pin key is the server identity plus the authorization scope and protocol version under
+which the definition was observed. The digest input is the definition only; scope and
+protocol version are comparison keys, not digest fields. A dual-era server may serve
+different tool sets in the legacy and modern eras (the official Everything server serves 16
+tools in legacy and 22 in modern), and a server may serve different tools to different
+authorization scopes. Do not compare a digest across scopes or eras.
